  "summary_en": "US federal regulation (14 CFR Part 47) setting requirements for registering aircraft and dealer registration certificates with the FAA: eligibility, ownership evidence, registration numbers, fees, expiration and renewal. Only passing unmanned-aircraft content (serial numbers for remote identification); no AI provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Aircraft may be registered only by eligible owners such as US citizens, resident aliens, and qualifying corporations.",
   "Applicants must submit Form 8050-1, evidence of ownership and a fee.",
   "Registration certificates expire after seven years and can be renewed.",
   "Section 47.14 requires unmanned aircraft serial numbers to follow Part 89 remote identification rules.",
   "Dealer's certificates permit flight testing and sales demonstrations and last one year."
